WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

2
00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:16.097
Listen. I'm from the Bronx.
so you need to keep it simple.

3
00:01:16.301 --> 00:01:20.465
Why is the bank buying all this
missile-guidance stuff from Calvini?

4
00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:23.568
I don't get it.

5
00:01:54.239 --> 00:01:55.866
The window will stay closed.

6
00:01:59.377 --> 00:02:00.708
You need to relax.

7
00:02:01.279 --> 00:02:04.077
I'm more comfortable tense.

8
00:02:05.283 --> 00:02:07.308
You came to us. remember?

9
00:02:07.519 --> 00:02:09.680
You wanted a way out
and I'm offering you one.

10
00:02:09.888 --> 00:02:12.652
I only met you 30 minutes ago...

11
00:02:12.857 --> 00:02:17.351
...and now you expect me just
to walk away from everything I know...

12
00:02:17.662 --> 00:02:19.688
...put my life in your hands.

13
00:02:21.367 --> 00:02:24.859
You want a little more time
to think things through. I get it...

14
00:02:25.304 --> 00:02:27.135
...but we're gonna need
another meet...

15
00:02:28.073 --> 00:02:30.234
...and I'm gonna need to
see some paper.

16
00:02:32.678 --> 00:02:35.841
Yes. Now get out of the car.

17
00:02:58.604 --> 00:02:59.662
<i>- Hey.
- Ella?</i>

18
00:02:59.872 --> 00:03:01.669
<i>- You done?
- Yeah. I just met with him.</i>

19
00:03:01.874 --> 00:03:04.172
<i>- And?
- Oh. he's real.</i>

20
00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:06.571
He's real enough
to blow this thing wide open.

21
00:03:06.779 --> 00:03:09.111
He told me the bank's
buying $200 million worth...

22
00:03:09.315 --> 00:03:11.180
...of missile-guidance systems.

23
00:03:11.417 --> 00:03:13.715
<i>- What do they need those for?
- I don't know.</i>

24
00:03:13.919 --> 00:03:15.352
<i>You gonna see him a second time?</i>

25
00:03:15.554 --> 00:03:19.752
Yeah. yeah. Listen. we're gonna meet
again. He's agreed to bring me paper.

26
00:03:19.959 --> 00:03:21.756
Right. I'll call you later.

27
00:03:22.194 --> 00:03:23.991
Thanks. Elle.

28
00:03:47.486 --> 00:03:48.783
Hey.

29
00:04:16.048 --> 00:04:19.540
Are you experiencing
any blurred or double vision?

30
00:04:20.252 --> 00:04:22.015
No.

31
00:04:23.122 --> 00:04:24.111
Nothing.

32
00:04:24.523 --> 00:04:25.922
Just follow the light. please.

33
00:04:31.931 --> 00:04:35.298
It's been noted that you were
experiencing ringing in your ears.

34
00:04:35.735 --> 00:04:36.724
Yes.

35
00:04:36.936 --> 00:04:39.769
Well. I would like to keep you here
overnight for observation.

36
00:04:39.973 --> 00:04:42.203
That won't be necessary.

37
00:04:45.879 --> 00:04:47.744
Where's my colleague?

38
00:04:51.918 --> 00:04:53.044
Thomas Schumer.

39
00:05:05.999 --> 00:05:07.523
It was definitely a heart attack?

40
00:05:09.636 --> 00:05:12.503
"Acute myocardial infarction." Yes.

41
00:05:26.986 --> 00:05:29.045
Your penlight. can I use it?

42
00:05:42.268 --> 00:05:43.257
What are you doing?

43
00:05:44.003 --> 00:05:45.527
Can you help me turn him over?

44
00:05:45.739 --> 00:05:48.572
- I'm afraid I can't allow you to...
- Just help me.

45
00:06:08.261 --> 00:06:11.697
We need to contact the Berlin police
and request an immediate autopsy.

46
00:06:11.898 --> 00:06:13.263
Why?

47
00:06:13.733 --> 00:06:16.725
Because I don't think this man
died of natural causes.

48
00:06:17.437 --> 00:06:18.631
Come on. Ella.

49
00:06:18.838 --> 00:06:21.898
If Schumer met this insider
in Berlin...

50
00:06:22.108 --> 00:06:24.770
...odds are this guy's
a foreign national. So it's federal.

51
00:06:24.978 --> 00:06:27.344
But you're not listening to me.
Let them meet again.

52
00:06:27.547 --> 00:06:30.015
The guy's gonna bring paper
and Tommy will close him.

53
00:06:30.216 --> 00:06:34.152
You still have to coordinate with
Justice if you want witness protection.

54
00:06:34.354 --> 00:06:37.084
I just tried both their cells again.
Straight to voicemail.

55
00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:38.450
Shit.

56
00:06:38.658 --> 00:06:41.991
I'm gonna try Tommy's wife at work.
If I have to bring DOJ into this...

57
00:06:42.196 --> 00:06:45.063
...they're gonna do what they've
always done with this.

58
00:06:45.266 --> 00:06:48.133
They're gonna stall us with red tape.
informant's gonna bolt...

59
00:06:48.335 --> 00:06:50.735
...and I'm telling you.
he could be the bombshell...

60
00:06:50.938 --> 00:06:53.463
...we've spent the last two years
looking for.

61
00:06:54.208 --> 00:06:55.971
Voicemail.

62
00:06:57.211 --> 00:06:59.577
What's going on?
Why aren't they calling us back?

63
00:06:59.780 --> 00:07:02.681
What do you want me to do?
I can't afford another turf war.

64
00:07:02.883 --> 00:07:06.819
- It's Salinger.
- Finally. Put him on speaker.

65
00:07:08.989 --> 00:07:12.425
Jesus. Lou.
What took you guys so long?

66
00:07:14.061 --> 00:07:16.461
Hello? You there?

67
00:07:16.664 --> 00:07:18.131
<i>Yeah.</i>

68
00:07:18.332 --> 00:07:20.266
So. what's up?

69
00:07:21.635 --> 00:07:23.626
<i>Tommy's dead.</i>

70
00:07:25.306 --> 00:07:26.500
What?

71
00:07:30.344 --> 00:07:32.039
<i>He's dead. Ella.</i>

72
00:07:32.246 --> 00:07:34.942
<i>I need you to get over here
as soon as you can.</i>

73
00:07:36.917 --> 00:07:40.546
Unnaturally red blood.
lambent membranes.

74
00:07:40.754 --> 00:07:42.984
Two key indicators
of hydrocyanic poisoning.

75
00:07:43.224 --> 00:07:44.691
This lesion on the neck...

76
00:07:44.892 --> 00:07:48.419
...is how the poison was introduced
into the bloodstream. percutaneously.

77
00:07:48.629 --> 00:07:50.654
The lesion tested negative
for any poison.

78
00:07:50.865 --> 00:07:54.323
There are any number of reasons
for this discoloration of the blood...

79
00:07:54.535 --> 00:07:56.503
...least likely of which
is hydrocyanic...

80
00:07:56.704 --> 00:07:58.695
I'm telling you. he was murdered.

81
00:08:05.546 --> 00:08:08.515
Well. I'm assuming
you suspect a combination...

82
00:08:08.716 --> 00:08:10.741
...of prussic acid and DMSO...

83
00:08:11.619 --> 00:08:14.144
...but then the reaction time
would have been immediate.

84
00:08:14.355 --> 00:08:16.152
Within one minute.

85
00:08:16.357 --> 00:08:19.121
Which means the killer
would have had to deliver the toxin...

86
00:08:19.326 --> 00:08:21.556
...after Schumer exited the car.

87
00:08:27.401 --> 00:08:30.598
So did you see anything unusual?

88
00:08:30.804 --> 00:08:33.329
Anybody approaching Schumer?

89
00:08:36.377 --> 00:08:38.607
No. I mean...

90
00:08:40.948 --> 00:08:42.711
I don't know.

91
00:08:43.150 --> 00:08:46.449
What is it that makes you so certain
he was assassinated?

92
00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:56.658
Agent Salinger and I have reason
to believe this might be connected...

93
00:08:56.865 --> 00:08:59.095
...to an ongoing investigation
being conducted...

94
00:08:59.301 --> 00:09:02.464
...by both my team at the Manhattan
DA's office and Interpol.

95
00:09:02.904 --> 00:09:05.270
- What investigation?
- I run a group at Interpol...

96
00:09:05.473 --> 00:09:08.931
...that focuses on financial operations
associated with organized crime.

97
00:09:09.477 --> 00:09:12.503
About two years ago. we began
receiving correlated intelligence...

98
00:09:12.714 --> 00:09:16.275
...regarding the illicit activities of
a bank based out of Luxembourg...

99
00:09:16.484 --> 00:09:18.782
...the International Bank
of Business and Credit.

100
00:09:18.987 --> 00:09:21.854
Under the direction of its chairman.
Jonas Skarssen...

101
00:09:22.057 --> 00:09:24.958
...we believe the IBBC has quietly
become the bank of choice...

102
00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:28.027
...for monies associated with
organized crime. capital flight...

103
00:09:28.229 --> 00:09:32.063
How is any of this related to Schumer
and the New York DA's office?

104
00:09:32.267 --> 00:09:33.632
The IBBC's Manhattan branch...

105
00:09:33.835 --> 00:09:36.827
...is the epicenter of its U.S.
money-laundering operation.

106
00:09:37.038 --> 00:09:39.506
Schumer and I
were working this case together.

107
00:09:39.708 --> 00:09:42.302
Agent Salinger and his department
have been assisting us.

108
00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:45.911
Why weren't we informed
of these details prior to this briefing?

109
00:10:06.501 --> 00:10:08.833
What was Schumer doing
here in Berlin?

110
00:10:09.237 --> 00:10:11.797
I set him up on a blind date
with an IBBC executive...

111
00:10:12.007 --> 00:10:14.999
...who was aware of our investigation
and looking to make a deal.

112
00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:17.371
And the identity of this informant?

113
00:10:17.579 --> 00:10:21.106
We don't know. He took precautions
to keep his identity anonymous.

114
00:10:21.616 --> 00:10:24.210
For the past 12 hours.
I've been trying hard to find him.

115
00:10:24.419 --> 00:10:27.547
I believe that if this man isn't
already dead. he soon will be.

116
00:10:27.956 --> 00:10:29.116
Why?

117
00:10:29.557 --> 00:10:31.889
Because. just like Schumer...

118
00:10:32.227 --> 00:10:34.889
...anyone that's in a position
to move against this bank...

119
00:10:35.096 --> 00:10:37.030
...has either ended up dead
or disappeared.

120
00:10:37.866 --> 00:10:41.996
Agent Salinger.
given your history with this matter...

121
00:10:42.203 --> 00:10:44.364
...I should think
you would be more careful...

122
00:10:44.572 --> 00:10:47.006
...before making
such extreme accusations.

123
00:10:47.208 --> 00:10:49.438
My history?
What are you talking about?

124
00:10:49.644 --> 00:10:51.635
We've reviewed your dossier.

125
00:10:52.514 --> 00:10:54.141
Have you?

126
00:10:55.483 --> 00:10:58.077
Well. that means you know
just about shit.

127
00:11:01.056 --> 00:11:06.256
I realize this is a trying time
for you both. but until I'm provided...

128
00:11:06.462 --> 00:11:09.659
...with something more compelling
than unsubstantiated theories...

129
00:11:10.433 --> 00:11:14.802
...pursuing the IBBC is simply
not going to happen here in Germany.

130
00:11:22.745 --> 00:11:25.213
Concorde Hotel. please.

131
00:11:30.753 --> 00:11:34.189
What was that back there? What
history was Diemer talking about?

132
00:11:34.390 --> 00:11:36.119
- Don't worry.
- Don't give me that shit.

133
00:11:36.325 --> 00:11:39.055
- What do they know that I don't?
- They don't know anything.

134
00:11:39.261 --> 00:11:40.694
Enough to get a rise out of you.

135
00:11:40.896 --> 00:11:44.559
I'm not getting into it.
You're so curious. read my file.

136
00:11:48.904 --> 00:11:51.896
I should never have let Tommy
walk into this.

137
00:11:52.675 --> 00:11:54.472
You didn't. I approved the meet.

138
00:11:54.677 --> 00:11:57.111
I was across the fucking street. Ella.

139
00:11:58.981 --> 00:12:01.142
I was right there.

140
00:12:04.120 --> 00:12:06.350
I saw him go down.

141
00:12:07.623 --> 00:12:09.215
I didn't see a thing.

142
00:12:14.563 --> 00:12:17.327
We won't let them bury this. Lou.

143
00:14:12.816 --> 00:14:15.341
This canvas appeals to you?

144
00:14:16.419 --> 00:14:18.887
I like the look of agony.

145
00:14:20.657 --> 00:14:22.284
Why?

146
00:14:23.260 --> 00:14:25.728
Because I know it's true.

147
00:14:34.571 --> 00:14:35.629
What am I doing here?

148
00:14:36.706 --> 00:14:39.436
Umberto Calvini is disengaging
from the deal.

149
00:14:39.976 --> 00:14:44.379
Your principle would like to bring
you in to troubleshoot the situation.

150
00:14:45.482 --> 00:14:49.441
If Calvini refuses to move forward. my
involvement won't make a difference.

151
00:14:49.653 --> 00:14:52.986
Your involvement would allow them
to appeal to Calvini's two sons...

152
00:14:53.189 --> 00:14:55.214
...who are much more open-minded.

153
00:14:56.626 --> 00:14:59.459
You'll find all the details in the file.

154
00:15:08.571 --> 00:15:11.597
I'll contact you
once negotiations are underway.

155
00:15:32.730 --> 00:15:34.823
IBBC executive dies
in freak road accident

156
00:15:49.113 --> 00:15:51.843
Luxembourg high society in shock
at death of Andre Clement

157
00:16:09.133 --> 00:16:10.498
Rene?

158
00:16:11.702 --> 00:16:13.727
What are you doing here so early?

159
00:16:13.938 --> 00:16:15.200
Salinger.

160
00:16:28.486 --> 00:16:29.680
I found the insider.

161
00:16:30.521 --> 00:16:31.681
What?

162
00:16:32.757 --> 00:16:35.692
I found the guy that Schumer
met with in Berlin.

163
00:16:36.861 --> 00:16:37.919
Andre Clement?

164
00:16:38.129 --> 00:16:41.189
The IBBC's senior vice president
of acquisitions.

165
00:16:46.570 --> 00:16:49.232
He was killed in a road accident
just outside Luxembourg...

166
00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:51.670
...approximately nine hours
after Schumer's death.

167
00:16:51.876 --> 00:16:54.572
And this is the gendarmerie's
preliminary accident report.

168
00:16:55.813 --> 00:16:58.008
He arrived in Berlin at 8 a. m...

169
00:16:58.949 --> 00:17:01.747
...on Luxair. Flight 9871
from Luxembourg.

170
00:17:02.319 --> 00:17:05.777
What doesn't track is in his statement.
the IBBC chairman. Jonas Skarssen...

171
00:17:05.990 --> 00:17:09.391
...claims that Clement had been with
him in Luxembourg since 10 a. m...

172
00:17:09.593 --> 00:17:13.290
...which is obviously impossible
if Clement arrived in Berlin at 8 a. m.

173
00:17:13.731 --> 00:17:16.598
Did the gendarmerie say anything
about this inconsistency?

174
00:17:17.368 --> 00:17:18.733
Nothing.

175
00:17:18.936 --> 00:17:20.699
- I haven't told them.
- What?

176
00:17:20.905 --> 00:17:23.533
I wanna go to Luxembourg
and question Skarssen myself.

177
00:17:23.741 --> 00:17:25.675
- No. Absolutely no.
- Viktor. listen to me.

178
00:17:25.876 --> 00:17:28.709
I go to Luxembourg.
Skarssen confirms that statement...

179
00:17:28.913 --> 00:17:30.881
...I catch him in that lie.
I can build...

180
00:17:31.082 --> 00:17:33.710
For chrissake. Lou.
you're not at the Yard anymore.

181
00:17:33.918 --> 00:17:36.580
Interpol is not
in the law-enforcement business.

182
00:17:37.455 --> 00:17:39.753
We deal in intelligence
and facilitation.

183
00:17:40.291 --> 00:17:44.422
Focus on that. work that and pass your
take onto the appropriate authorities.

184
00:17:44.629 --> 00:17:45.721
And then what?

185
00:17:46.932 --> 00:17:50.231
You know we've been circulating
our take since the very beginning.

186
00:17:50.435 --> 00:17:52.596
No one ever does anything.
no one ever can.

187
00:17:52.804 --> 00:17:56.467
Whatever case we have gets lost
in the complexities of international law.

188
00:17:57.642 --> 00:18:01.339
Schumer. Clement...

189
00:18:01.546 --> 00:18:04.140
...this entire fucking wall.

190
00:18:04.783 --> 00:18:07.980
There's nothing that complex
about cold-blooded murder.

191
00:18:27.873 --> 00:18:29.966
Hi. I've got an appointment
with Mr. Skarssen.

192
00:18:30.175 --> 00:18:34.305
- Your name. please?
- Mr. Salinger? Please follow me.

193
00:19:16.755 --> 00:19:17.744
Mr. Skarssen.

194
00:19:23.228 --> 00:19:24.889
Mr. Skarssen.

195
00:19:31.570 --> 00:19:33.697
Agent Salinger? Please follow me.

196
00:19:51.289 --> 00:19:53.190
Mr. White.

197
00:19:53.492 --> 00:19:56.689
Agent Salinger.
I apologize for the wait.

198
00:19:56.896 --> 00:19:59.865
I'm Martin White.
the IBBC's legal counsel.

199
00:20:00.066 --> 00:20:02.364
This is Commissioner Villon
of the gendarmerie.

200
00:20:02.568 --> 00:20:06.265
I thought it useful for him to join us.
considering the nature of your query.

201
00:20:06.472 --> 00:20:08.064
Please. have a seat.

202
00:20:09.742 --> 00:20:11.972
I think there's
some misunderstanding.

203
00:20:12.178 --> 00:20:14.976
I'm here to speak with Mr. Skarssen.

204
00:20:15.181 --> 00:20:19.447
Yes. but as Mr. Skarssen's attorney.
I insisted that I speak with you first.

205
00:20:19.885 --> 00:20:23.286
Mr. White. I had a confirmed meeting
with Mr. Skarssen at 11:00.

206
00:20:23.689 --> 00:20:26.556
If I was gonna meet with you first.
why didn't anybody tell me?

207
00:20:26.759 --> 00:20:29.353
I understand.
and I'm sorry for the confusion...

208
00:20:29.562 --> 00:20:32.622
...but I'm sure I can help
answer your questions.

209
00:20:32.832 --> 00:20:35.596
Now. please. have a seat.

210
00:20:56.289 --> 00:20:57.517
As I'm sure you're aware...

211
00:20:57.723 --> 00:20:59.953
...I have some questions
regarding Andre Clement.

212
00:21:00.793 --> 00:21:02.192
Yes.

213
00:21:03.462 --> 00:21:05.862
It's my understanding
that Mr. Clement was working...

214
00:21:06.065 --> 00:21:09.000
...at Mr. Skarssen's residence
the night he was killed.

215
00:21:09.201 --> 00:21:11.692
The night of the accident. yes.

216
00:21:12.805 --> 00:21:15.171
What time did he arrive
at Skarssen's home that day?

217
00:21:15.374 --> 00:21:18.741
If I recall correctly. around 6 p. m.

218
00:21:21.814 --> 00:21:24.146
- You were there?
- Yes.

219
00:21:25.785 --> 00:21:27.412
And you're certain about this time?

220
00:21:28.387 --> 00:21:29.911
Quite.

221
00:21:30.489 --> 00:21:32.218
I'm confused.

222
00:21:33.693 --> 00:21:36.457
What you're telling me conflicts
with Skarssen's statement...

223
00:21:36.662 --> 00:21:38.823
...in the gendarmerie's
accident report...

224
00:21:39.031 --> 00:21:42.125
...which was that Clement had been
working with him since 10 a. m.

225
00:21:43.169 --> 00:21:45.467
I was present when Mr. Skarssen
gave his statement.

226
00:21:45.671 --> 00:21:48.697
- That is not what he said.
- It is according to this report.

227
00:21:50.543 --> 00:21:52.170
May I?

228
00:22:10.964 --> 00:22:13.023
There is an error
in the preliminary draft.

229
00:22:13.233 --> 00:22:14.222
The time is wrong.

230
00:22:15.969 --> 00:22:19.769
The finalized report here
says Clement arrived at 6 p. m.

231
00:22:20.407 --> 00:22:23.376
Clerical errors like this
can happen from time to time.

232
00:22:23.577 --> 00:22:26.045
This is why the gendarmerie
discourages the release...

233
00:22:26.246 --> 00:22:29.443
...of any preliminary documentation
pertaining to open cases.

234
00:22:31.518 --> 00:22:35.113
So is there anything else
we can do for you. Agent Salinger?

235
00:22:45.632 --> 00:22:46.621
<i>- Yeah.
- It's me.</i>

236
00:22:46.833 --> 00:22:49.666
<i>I just got the results from
the tox analysis I ran on Schumer.</i>

237
00:22:49.870 --> 00:22:52.862
<i>- And?
- It's inconclusive.</i>

238
00:22:53.073 --> 00:22:55.507
Inconclusive? What the hell
is that supposed to mean?

239
00:22:55.709 --> 00:22:58.269
<i>They found trace elements
of cyanide in his blood...</i>

240
00:22:58.478 --> 00:23:00.571
<i>... but the levels
are not nearly high enough...</i>

241
00:23:00.781 --> 00:23:03.215
<i>... to meet their criteria
for poisoning.</i>

242
00:23:05.085 --> 00:23:06.279
<i>Are you there?</i>

243
00:23:25.338 --> 00:23:26.930
Sorry.

244
00:23:29.309 --> 00:23:31.277
I'm sorry.

245
00:23:34.481 --> 00:23:36.574
Are you crazy?

246
00:23:59.873 --> 00:24:01.135
Madame Clement?

247
00:24:04.211 --> 00:24:07.374
It's Eleanor Whitman from the
New York District Attorney's office.

248
00:24:08.148 --> 00:24:10.514
I already left a couple
messages just...

249
00:24:29.737 --> 00:24:31.898
Mrs. Clement.
I'm sorry to keep calling you.

250
00:24:32.106 --> 00:24:35.542
I can only imagine what a difficult time
this must be for you.

251
00:24:36.511 --> 00:24:40.311
But I'm not convinced your
husband's death was an accident.

252
00:24:42.383 --> 00:24:44.044
Look. here's my cell number.

253
00:24:44.252 --> 00:24:49.485
001-917-135-6565.

254
00:24:49.690 --> 00:24:51.089
You can call any time...

255
00:24:51.292 --> 00:24:55.752
<i>Stop calling me. I have nothing
to say to you. Just leave me alone.</i>

256
00:24:55.963 --> 00:24:58.761
Please. I just need to ask you
a few questions.

257
00:24:58.966 --> 00:25:01.594
<i>I have two children.
They've already lost their father.</i>

258
00:25:01.802 --> 00:25:05.761
<i>- I understand.
- No. you don't.</i>

259
00:25:08.075 --> 00:25:10.600
Are you aware your husband
met with our investigators...

260
00:25:10.811 --> 00:25:12.540
...the day he was killed?

261
00:25:20.555 --> 00:25:22.386
You ever planning to come to bed?

262
00:25:23.190 --> 00:25:25.750
- I heard your voice.
- I'm sorry.

263
00:25:25.960 --> 00:25:28.394
- When'd he come in here?
- An hour ago.

264
00:25:29.096 --> 00:25:30.859
<i>T. rex was in the closet again.</i>

265
00:25:32.333 --> 00:25:34.198
Let me take him back.

266
00:25:34.969 --> 00:25:36.869
Come on. buddy.

267
00:27:15.737 --> 00:27:16.726
Lou?

268
00:27:17.339 --> 00:27:19.398
They knew about
the discrepancy in the report.

269
00:27:19.608 --> 00:27:22.099
They had Skarssen's
statement changed.

270
00:27:22.310 --> 00:27:23.675
How did they know. Viktor?

271
00:27:24.880 --> 00:27:25.904
- Come inside.
- No.

272
00:27:28.483 --> 00:27:31.043
Are you insane? It's freezing out.

273
00:27:31.386 --> 00:27:32.717
Come outside.

274
00:27:32.921 --> 00:27:34.479
Stop it!

275
00:27:41.863 --> 00:27:43.626
Lou. wait.

276
00:27:45.200 --> 00:27:46.224
Lou.

277
00:27:49.137 --> 00:27:51.230
Have you lost your mind?

278
00:28:05.287 --> 00:28:07.687
I think we take the dog for a walk.

279
00:28:08.056 --> 00:28:10.047
Get some fresh air.

280
00:28:21.870 --> 00:28:23.428
Who did this?

281
00:28:23.638 --> 00:28:24.969
Who do you think?

282
00:28:26.108 --> 00:28:27.234
From my apartment.

283
00:28:27.943 --> 00:28:30.070
Whitman's got them too.

284
00:28:30.612 --> 00:28:33.012
We need to inform
the secretary general immediately.

285
00:28:33.215 --> 00:28:34.375
You gotta be kidding.

286
00:28:34.583 --> 00:28:37.211
We start setting off alarms.
the opportunity will be lost.

287
00:28:37.419 --> 00:28:38.443
Opportunity?

288
00:28:38.653 --> 00:28:40.246
The last thing Schumer told Ella...

289
00:28:40.456 --> 00:28:44.825
...was that Clement was giving him
information on an IBBC arms deal.

290
00:28:47.096 --> 00:28:48.256
Umberto Calvini.

291
00:28:48.464 --> 00:28:51.729
Chairman of Calvini Defense. one
of the largest defense contractors.

292
00:28:51.934 --> 00:28:54.334
And probably
Italy's next prime minister.

293
00:28:54.537 --> 00:28:57.233
This guy standing next to him.
that's our insider.

294
00:28:58.141 --> 00:28:59.301
Andre Clement.

295
00:29:00.143 --> 00:29:01.633
And?

296
00:29:01.844 --> 00:29:04.711
Whitman found out that Clement
was negotiating for the IBBC...

297
00:29:04.914 --> 00:29:07.280
...to purchase a large number
of missile guidance...

298
00:29:07.483 --> 00:29:09.644
...and control systems
from Calvini Defense.

299
00:29:09.852 --> 00:29:12.252
But at the very last minute.
the deal collapsed.

300
00:29:12.455 --> 00:29:13.444
What happened?

301
00:29:13.656 --> 00:29:16.784
We don't know. Whitman's
meeting me in Milan tomorrow.

302
00:29:16.993 --> 00:29:18.927
We're gonna talk to Calvini
and find out.

303
00:31:02.299 --> 00:31:04.096
- Hey.
- Hey.

304
00:31:05.035 --> 00:31:07.333
Eleanor Whitman.
this is Inspector Alberto Cerutti.

305
00:31:07.537 --> 00:31:09.562
- Charmed.
- Nice to meet you.

306
00:31:09.773 --> 00:31:11.138
Please. there's not much time.

307
00:31:11.341 --> 00:31:13.969
Calvini leaves for Turin
immediately after this engagement.

308
00:31:14.177 --> 00:31:16.668
I didn't realize we were meeting
at a political rally.

309
00:31:16.880 --> 00:31:19.474
Best we could do
on such short notice.

310
00:31:23.787 --> 00:31:26.688
Thirtieth floor. I'll be waiting outside.

311
00:31:35.399 --> 00:31:36.764
You need to press the button.

312
00:31:43.640 --> 00:31:45.631
You look awful.

313
00:31:45.842 --> 00:31:47.810
Thanks.

314
00:31:49.579 --> 00:31:51.740
When was the last time
you got any sleep?

315
00:31:52.149 --> 00:31:53.810
Don't know.

316
00:31:56.820 --> 00:31:59.015
When was the last time
you had a healthy meal?

317
00:31:59.489 --> 00:32:01.150
Can't remember.

318
00:32:02.592 --> 00:32:06.528
- How about the last time you got laid?
- Why. are you offering?

319
00:32:07.764 --> 00:32:10.790
You need to take better care
of yourself. Lou.

320
00:32:11.001 --> 00:32:14.801
I can't have you crash and burn
like you did two years ago.

321
00:32:17.441 --> 00:32:19.170
Please follow me.

322
00:32:20.110 --> 00:32:21.941
This meeting is strictly off the record.

323
00:32:22.145 --> 00:32:25.444
Mr. Calvini cannot be entangled
in your investigation...

324
00:32:25.649 --> 00:32:29.608
...nor can his participation in this
discussion find its way to the press.

325
00:32:29.820 --> 00:32:30.809
We understand.

326
00:32:31.455 --> 00:32:33.855
Wait here for a moment.

327
00:32:35.625 --> 00:32:37.889
So you read my file.

328
00:32:38.395 --> 00:32:40.522
I made a few calls to London.

329
00:32:41.031 --> 00:32:42.623
You should've told me everything...

330
00:32:42.833 --> 00:32:46.735
...with your IBBC case at the Yard.
You should've told me it's why you left.

331
00:32:47.371 --> 00:32:49.236
What did they tell you?

332
00:32:50.140 --> 00:32:53.166
That you screwed up because
the witness you brought in was a joke.

333
00:32:53.377 --> 00:32:56.210
And when you were forced to
drop him. the case fell apart.

334
00:32:56.413 --> 00:32:59.746
You flipped out. attacked the assistant
commissioner and broke his nose.

335
00:32:59.950 --> 00:33:03.512
My case did not fall apart. it was shut
down. and my witness was rock-solid.

336
00:33:04.288 --> 00:33:06.654
He gave us everything we needed
against the bank...

337
00:33:06.858 --> 00:33:10.157
...and then suddenly. out of nowhere.
my AC forced me to cut him loose.

338
00:33:10.361 --> 00:33:13.091
Three days later.
they all died in a car crash.

339
00:33:15.166 --> 00:33:17.691
- "They"?
- He had a wife and two kids.

340
00:33:20.204 --> 00:33:23.833
Mr. Calvini. we'd like to know
why the IBBC. a bank...

341
00:33:24.042 --> 00:33:27.307
...would be purchasing millions
of dollars worth of missile guidance...

342
00:33:27.512 --> 00:33:29.343
...and control systems
from your company.

343
00:33:32.050 --> 00:33:35.247
The IBBC has purchased
billions of dollars worth...

344
00:33:35.453 --> 00:33:39.355
...of Silkworm missiles from
the People's Republic of China...

345
00:33:39.557 --> 00:33:42.685
...which they have presold
to clients in the Middle East...

346
00:33:42.894 --> 00:33:44.452
...contingent upon the missiles...

347
00:33:44.662 --> 00:33:47.290
...being equipped
with VOLCON guidance systems.

348
00:33:47.899 --> 00:33:52.302
My company's one of only two in the
world which produce the VOLCON.

349
00:33:52.503 --> 00:33:56.769
- Who's the other?
- Sunay. Ahmet Sunay.

350
00:33:56.974 --> 00:33:58.566
Of Turkish Aerotech?

351
00:34:00.244 --> 00:34:03.145
But why is the bank committing
so much capital and resources...

352
00:34:03.347 --> 00:34:05.542
...to the sale of these missiles?

353
00:34:09.887 --> 00:34:10.876
It's a test.

354
00:34:12.990 --> 00:34:14.753
Small arms
are the only weapons used...

355
00:34:14.959 --> 00:34:18.258
...in 99 percent
of the world's conflicts...

356
00:34:18.930 --> 00:34:21.398
...and no one has the capacity
to manufacture them...

357
00:34:21.599 --> 00:34:24.397
...faster and cheaper than China.

358
00:34:24.969 --> 00:34:27.267
What Skarssen is attempting to do...

359
00:34:27.738 --> 00:34:30.832
...is to make the IBBC
the exclusive broker...

360
00:34:31.242 --> 00:34:34.678
...of Chinese small arms
to the Third World.

361
00:34:35.279 --> 00:34:38.510
And the missile deal
is the gateway transaction.

362
00:34:38.916 --> 00:34:42.647
Yeah. but billions of dollars invested
simply to be a broker?

363
00:34:42.854 --> 00:34:44.515
There can't be much profit for them.

364
00:34:44.722 --> 00:34:48.419
No. This is not about making profit
from weapon sales.

365
00:34:50.228 --> 00:34:52.253
It's about control.

366
00:34:53.564 --> 00:34:57.432
Control the flow of weapons.
control the conflict.

367
00:34:57.635 --> 00:34:59.034
No.

368
00:35:00.004 --> 00:35:02.802
No. no. The IBBC is a bank.

369
00:35:03.307 --> 00:35:06.743
Their objective isn't
to control the conflict...

370
00:35:06.944 --> 00:35:10.311
...it's to control the debt
that the conflict produces.

371
00:35:10.882 --> 00:35:14.284
You see. the real value
of a conflict...

372
00:35:14.486 --> 00:35:15.783
...the true value...

373
00:35:16.221 --> 00:35:19.019
...is in the debt that it creates.

374
00:35:19.224 --> 00:35:21.454
You control the debt...

375
00:35:22.294 --> 00:35:24.387
...you control everything.

376
00:35:26.632 --> 00:35:28.896
You find this upsetting. yes?

377
00:35:29.601 --> 00:35:33.264
But this is the very essence
of the banking industry...

378
00:35:33.505 --> 00:35:38.670
...to make us all.
whether we be nations or individuals...

379
00:35:38.877 --> 00:35:41.175
...slaves to debt.

380
00:35:42.181 --> 00:35:44.843
You sound like
you're not very fond of the IBBC.

381
00:35:46.051 --> 00:35:47.916
What happened?

382
00:35:49.555 --> 00:35:51.648
I was fond of Andre Clement.

383
00:35:52.424 --> 00:35:54.324
I trusted him...

384
00:35:54.526 --> 00:35:56.187
...and he was a good friend.

385
00:36:04.169 --> 00:36:07.434
Then help us make sure
he didn't die in vain.

386
00:36:09.308 --> 00:36:11.208
Find me after the speech.

387
00:36:11.410 --> 00:36:13.844
We can talk in the car
on my way to the airport.

388
00:36:29.094 --> 00:36:31.494
Umberto Calvini.

389
00:38:06.092 --> 00:38:07.889
Definitely connected to any...

390
00:38:20.840 --> 00:38:22.467
What the hell is going on?

391
00:38:22.709 --> 00:38:24.199
They shot him!

392
00:39:24.070 --> 00:39:26.231
Secure this area
and block all exits. now.

393
00:39:26.439 --> 00:39:28.031
Go!

394
00:41:03.770 --> 00:41:06.136
Oh. my God. Are you all right?

395
00:41:06.340 --> 00:41:07.329
I think so.

396
00:41:07.541 --> 00:41:09.805
Take that left.
Maybe you can cut him off.

397
00:41:10.010 --> 00:41:11.477
Go.

398
00:41:12.179 --> 00:41:13.203
Go!

399
00:42:21.749 --> 00:42:22.738
Turn off the engine...

400
00:42:22.951 --> 00:42:25.317
...and stick your hands
out of the window!

401
00:42:26.254 --> 00:42:27.482
Turn off the engine...

402
00:42:27.689 --> 00:42:30.715
...and stick your hands
out of the window! Now!

403
00:42:48.009 --> 00:42:52.673
Our relationship with the Swiss has
become impossible over the past year.

404
00:42:52.880 --> 00:42:54.814
They are discounting
our dollar deposits...

405
00:42:55.016 --> 00:42:57.382
...by 160 basis points below par.

406
00:42:57.585 --> 00:42:59.849
They have doubled the cost
of moving our money.

407
00:43:00.054 --> 00:43:02.784
Well. general. what do you expect?

408
00:43:03.024 --> 00:43:04.821
You've been in the jungle
long enough...

409
00:43:05.026 --> 00:43:08.052
...to know that when the lion kills.
it's the jackal that profits.

410
00:43:08.262 --> 00:43:09.729
Yes.

411
00:43:10.398 --> 00:43:12.229
The IBBC is specifically structured...

412
00:43:12.433 --> 00:43:15.300
...to handle the particular needs
of your type of organization.

413
00:43:15.837 --> 00:43:18.829
We can give you better rates
and terms than other competitors...

414
00:43:19.907 --> 00:43:21.465
...but we can offer you much more:

415
00:43:22.343 --> 00:43:23.332
Weapons...

416
00:43:23.845 --> 00:43:26.279
...intelligence. logistical support...

417
00:43:26.481 --> 00:43:28.881
...everything that
the Revolutionary Freedom Front...

418
00:43:29.083 --> 00:43:31.074
...would need to revive itself.

419
00:43:31.319 --> 00:43:33.480
But in exchange for what?

420
00:43:33.688 --> 00:43:37.180
You must understand.
the RFF has no money.

421
00:43:40.094 --> 00:43:45.157
Money is not this institution's
primary medium of exchange.

422
00:43:48.636 --> 00:43:51.127
What are you proposing exactly?

423
00:43:51.839 --> 00:43:54.740
We believe that. with the right kind
of direction and support...

424
00:43:54.942 --> 00:43:58.036
...the RFF could become a very
influential force in your country.

425
00:43:58.646 --> 00:43:59.874
Perhaps potent enough...

426
00:44:00.081 --> 00:44:03.279
...to stage a successful coup
in the coming months.

427
00:44:05.421 --> 00:44:07.616
And if this were possible...

428
00:44:08.057 --> 00:44:10.958
...what does your bank
hope to gain from it?

429
00:44:13.395 --> 00:44:18.094
The gratitude and consideration
of a very influential friend.

430
00:44:19.802 --> 00:44:21.531
Excuse me.

431
00:44:22.104 --> 00:44:24.732
Mr. White and Mr. Ehames
asked me to interrupt.

432
00:44:26.575 --> 00:44:29.305
Would you excuse me. general?
I'll be right back.

433
00:44:42.491 --> 00:44:43.788
What is it?

434
00:44:49.198 --> 00:44:52.531
Approximately 30 minutes ago.
Umberto Calvini was assassinated...

435
00:44:52.735 --> 00:44:55.966
...while giving a speech
at a political rally in Milan.

436
00:44:59.408 --> 00:45:00.932
We've been discussing it.

437
00:45:01.376 --> 00:45:04.812
I think we should wait until
the authorities resolve the matter...

438
00:45:05.013 --> 00:45:08.414
...and then approach the sons
to revive negotiations.

439
00:45:09.084 --> 00:45:10.142
How long will this take?

440
00:45:10.352 --> 00:45:14.254
I've been assured the investigation
will move swiftly...

441
00:45:15.257 --> 00:45:19.557
...but unexpected fallout of an event
like this can always complicate things.

442
00:45:19.762 --> 00:45:22.196
We only have 60 days left
to deliver the worms.

443
00:45:22.397 --> 00:45:23.955
There's no time for complications.

444
00:45:24.166 --> 00:45:27.260
That's a risk you take
with such an ambitious agenda.

445
00:45:27.903 --> 00:45:30.872
I don't foresee any problems.
Had it not been for their father...

446
00:45:31.073 --> 00:45:34.065
...Mario and Enzo Calvini
would have made our deal long ago.

447
00:45:34.276 --> 00:45:36.676
Now there's no reason
for them not to move forward.

448
00:45:37.880 --> 00:45:41.111
An important man and devoted father
has just been killed.

449
00:45:43.285 --> 00:45:45.753
I suggest that we send a letter
to Calvini's family...

450
00:45:45.954 --> 00:45:49.913
...extending our heartfelt prayers
and condolences for their terrible loss.

451
00:45:51.226 --> 00:45:52.750
I don't know. but I'm okay.

452
00:45:52.961 --> 00:45:55.327
The doctors
checked me out thoroughly.

453
00:45:56.064 --> 00:45:57.964
Kiss Jake for me. will you?

454
00:46:05.440 --> 00:46:08.637
So the shooter was identified
as a member of the Red Brigade.

455
00:46:08.844 --> 00:46:10.539
What about the guy in the car?

456
00:46:10.746 --> 00:46:13.944
Car was stolen. They were unable
to lift prints. fibers or residue...

457
00:46:14.150 --> 00:46:17.381
...or locate any witnesses
who saw him exiting the vehicle.

458
00:46:17.587 --> 00:46:19.646
- So?
- So the carabinieri are announcing...

459
00:46:19.856 --> 00:46:21.721
...that the Red Brigade
was responsible...

460
00:46:21.925 --> 00:46:24.519
...for the assassination
at the press conference tonight.

461
00:46:24.727 --> 00:46:26.957
We're not convinced
the Red Brigade's behind this.

462
00:46:27.163 --> 00:46:29.893
Someone could simply be
making it appear as though they are.

463
00:46:31.234 --> 00:46:32.633
This isn't my case...

464
00:46:32.836 --> 00:46:35.805
...and the man in charge
of the investigation is very powerful...

465
00:46:36.005 --> 00:46:37.199
...and a real bastard.

466
00:46:37.407 --> 00:46:40.672
All we wanna do
is just look around a little.

467
00:47:03.766 --> 00:47:05.427
- Antonio.
- Alberto.

468
00:47:05.969 --> 00:47:07.266
Just a moment.

469
00:47:35.098 --> 00:47:37.032
They done
the trajectory analysis yet?

470
00:47:38.167 --> 00:47:40.260
Cerutti said no.

471
00:49:00.317 --> 00:49:03.548
If there was a second shooter.
he could've positioned himself here.

472
00:49:05.322 --> 00:49:07.051
The stopwatch they found
in the room...

473
00:49:07.257 --> 00:49:09.282
...it was set on
a one-minute countdown. yes?

474
00:49:09.493 --> 00:49:12.951
Right. Calvini was killed a little
over one minute into his speech.

475
00:49:13.764 --> 00:49:16.198
What if this was all synchronized?

476
00:49:20.004 --> 00:49:21.665
Okay...

477
00:49:23.440 --> 00:49:25.169
...let's say I'm the second shooter.

478
00:49:26.643 --> 00:49:28.338
<i>The guy below
doesn't know I'm here...</i>

479
00:49:28.545 --> 00:49:31.173
<i>... but I'm positioned
right above his room.</i>

480
00:49:32.483 --> 00:49:36.146
<i>I'm armed with a Sauer 200 rifle.
just like he is.</i>

481
00:49:37.054 --> 00:49:39.488
I have a stopwatch set
on a one-minute countdown...

482
00:49:39.690 --> 00:49:42.056
<i>... which I start when Calvini
begins his speech.</i>

483
00:49:42.259 --> 00:49:44.727
The sniper below has been instructed
to do the same...

484
00:49:44.928 --> 00:49:47.590
...because that's when
he's gonna fire his first bullet.

485
00:49:47.798 --> 00:49:52.098
If he misses. I'm ready to
follow through with one of my own.

486
00:49:52.936 --> 00:49:54.995
The sniper fires. misses.

487
00:49:55.372 --> 00:49:56.771
<i>Seconds later...</i>

488
00:49:58.075 --> 00:49:59.838
...I take Calvini out with a headshot.

489
00:50:01.512 --> 00:50:04.140
It's a good theory.
but there's one problem.

490
00:50:04.348 --> 00:50:06.009
Why?

491
00:50:08.585 --> 00:50:11.053
Two shots were fired
from the window...

492
00:50:11.255 --> 00:50:13.018
<i>... two slugs were recovered...</i>

493
00:50:13.223 --> 00:50:15.521
...and two casings were found
next to the gun...

494
00:50:15.726 --> 00:50:19.287
...ballistics confirming that the casings
came from the gun in the hotel room.

495
00:50:19.496 --> 00:50:22.556
<i>So if the kill shot came from
a second shooter here on the roof...</i>

496
00:50:22.766 --> 00:50:25.428
...that'd be a total
of three bullets fired.

497
00:50:25.636 --> 00:50:27.934
How do you explain
the absence of the third bullet?

498
00:50:30.574 --> 00:50:32.337
I can't.

499
00:51:00.605 --> 00:51:03.005
I think I've seen this print before.

500
00:51:03.708 --> 00:51:05.232
Where?

501
00:51:05.443 --> 00:51:07.172
Hanging on the wall of my office.

502
00:51:22.660 --> 00:51:26.426
So this was lifted from the scene of the
Stefan Heuss hit in Brussels last year.

503
00:51:26.631 --> 00:51:28.724
A former IMF executive director.

504
00:51:28.933 --> 00:51:31.163
Has he ever seen
a tread pattern like this before?

505
00:51:39.844 --> 00:51:43.541
He believes it came from
a custom shoe made for a leg brace.

506
00:51:43.748 --> 00:51:45.773
The braces are typically
made out of steel...

507
00:51:45.984 --> 00:51:47.952
...or alloy.
but the condition of the leg...

508
00:51:48.153 --> 00:51:50.519
...would determine the specific
type of device used.

509
00:51:52.757 --> 00:51:54.952
He says that the prints
are a probable match.

510
00:51:57.662 --> 00:52:01.098
Please get these over to Alan Kovacs
at FBI Impressions right away...

511
00:52:01.299 --> 00:52:03.995
...and make sure
he has my contact numbers.

512
00:52:05.003 --> 00:52:06.630
Thanks.

513
00:52:07.672 --> 00:52:10.368
Ella. if the FBI confirms
that these prints are a match...

514
00:52:10.575 --> 00:52:12.975
...it means the bank's
used the same assassin twice.

515
00:52:13.945 --> 00:52:17.847
Which means if we can get him.
we can get the bank.

516
00:52:52.418 --> 00:52:53.680
What was that?

517
00:52:58.390 --> 00:53:01.951
<i>That was Capitano Barillo. the man
in charge of the Calvini investigation.</i>

518
00:53:02.161 --> 00:53:05.358
- What did he want?
- My ass on a platter...

519
00:53:05.564 --> 00:53:07.862
...and both of you
on the next flight out of Milan.

520
00:53:08.267 --> 00:53:10.235
Didn't you tell him
what we just found?

521
00:53:10.436 --> 00:53:11.903
I tried.

522
00:53:12.104 --> 00:53:15.096
Fuck him.
He can't force us to leave.

523
00:53:15.307 --> 00:53:17.901
He has already spoken
to your superiors.

524
00:53:18.110 --> 00:53:20.237
You have both been ordered home.

525
00:53:21.146 --> 00:53:22.943
Arnie. you can't just sit there...

526
00:53:23.148 --> 00:53:25.241
...and lecture me
about protocol and procedure.

527
00:53:25.451 --> 00:53:27.214
You know what's happening here.

528
00:53:27.419 --> 00:53:29.910
Well. who gives a shit
about jurisdictional provenance?

529
00:53:30.122 --> 00:53:32.317
We just had a major breakthrough.

530
00:53:33.559 --> 00:53:36.392
That's great. Arnie.
You're a real stand-up guy.

531
00:53:36.595 --> 00:53:38.722
This is total bullshit.

532
00:53:39.331 --> 00:53:41.231
I wish I could have
been more helpful.

533
00:53:41.433 --> 00:53:43.367
Oh. no. you've been great. Alberto.

534
00:53:43.569 --> 00:53:46.504
I'm gonna do everything I can
to take the heat off you.

535
00:53:47.006 --> 00:53:48.371
Thanks.

536
00:53:49.341 --> 00:53:52.742
Thanks for everything.
Sorry for all the trouble we caused.

537
00:54:05.090 --> 00:54:06.079
What?

538
00:54:06.292 --> 00:54:08.692
His leg brace would be made
of metal. right?

539
00:54:09.528 --> 00:54:12.258
- So?
- So if he left through an airport...

540
00:54:12.464 --> 00:54:14.659
...security would have made him
show it to them.

541
00:54:33.919 --> 00:54:35.511
That's definitely him.

542
00:54:35.721 --> 00:54:39.384
- He doesn't look like much.
- I think that's the idea.

543
00:54:40.159 --> 00:54:41.786
Seems to know
where the cameras are.

544
00:54:41.994 --> 00:54:44.963
Look how he always angles his face
just out of our line of sight.

545
00:54:45.164 --> 00:54:46.563
Even if you do find him...

546
00:54:46.765 --> 00:54:49.962
...that's not enough evidence to
convict the man without a confession.

547
00:54:50.169 --> 00:54:53.400
If we find him. prosecution will be
irrelevant. He'll be a marked man.

548
00:54:53.605 --> 00:54:56.335
He can either die for the bank
or flip for us.

549
00:54:57.276 --> 00:55:01.714
I got him. He is traveling under
the name Sherwood. Timothy M.

550
00:55:01.915 --> 00:55:06.045
He boarded Flight Alitalia 422.
departing Milan at 6 p. m. yesterday...

551
00:55:06.252 --> 00:55:08.686
...and arriving in New York
at JFK at 10 p. m.

552
00:55:11.091 --> 00:55:13.059
What time's the next flight
to New York?

553
00:55:53.733 --> 00:55:57.066
Detectives Hubbard. Ward. Ornelas.
this is Agent Lou Salinger.

554
00:55:57.270 --> 00:55:58.328
- Finally.
- How you doing?

555
00:55:58.538 --> 00:56:01.063
- Let me take that.
- Thanks. So. what do we have?

556
00:56:01.274 --> 00:56:02.400
Well. we got lucky.

557
00:56:03.276 --> 00:56:06.211
Some clip shots of him
moving through customs.

558
00:56:06.413 --> 00:56:08.244
That's a good one.

559
00:56:09.749 --> 00:56:13.708
The Sherwood ID he used? It's clean.
All of it attached to a dead address.

560
00:56:13.920 --> 00:56:15.717
Where'd he go
after he cleared customs?

561
00:56:15.922 --> 00:56:18.755
Don't know.
CCTV footage lost him at the curb.

562
00:56:18.958 --> 00:56:21.950
We canvassed all the limousine
and taxicab companies in the city.

563
00:56:22.162 --> 00:56:26.064
Airport parking. rental agencies.
Didn't come up with shit.

564
00:56:26.266 --> 00:56:28.325
There's a chance
he might live in the city.

565
00:56:28.535 --> 00:56:29.661
Why is that?

566
00:56:30.336 --> 00:56:32.736
Kovacs from FBI Impressions called.

567
00:56:33.406 --> 00:56:38.002
"The footprint was left by a shoe
used for knee-ankle-foot orthosis.

568
00:56:38.411 --> 00:56:41.175
The tread pattern is exclusive
to shoes produced...

569
00:56:41.381 --> 00:56:44.646
...at the Isaacson Orthopedic Institute
here in the city."

570
00:56:44.851 --> 00:56:46.785
The shoe could have only come
from there.

571
00:56:46.986 --> 00:56:49.147
Do you have a contact person
to run down?

572
00:56:49.355 --> 00:56:50.947
We got Dr. Isaacson.

573
00:56:52.459 --> 00:56:55.758
All right. You guys go check it out.
I'm expected at the office.

574
00:56:55.962 --> 00:56:56.951
Hubb?

575
00:56:57.163 --> 00:57:00.291
Get ready for the smackdown.
He's gonna come at you hard.

576
00:57:43.878 --> 00:57:46.540
- Who is it?
- N.Y.P.D.

577
00:57:49.350 --> 00:57:50.942
- Dr. Isaacson?
- Yeah.

578
00:57:51.151 --> 00:57:54.245
Detective Ornelas. N.Y.P.D.
This is my partner. Detective Ward.

579
00:57:54.455 --> 00:57:56.685
- We'd like to ask a couple questions.
- Why?

580
00:57:57.057 --> 00:57:58.615
What do you want?
Why are you here?

581
00:57:58.826 --> 00:58:02.455
Calm down. We just wanna ask you
a few questions about a patient.

582
00:58:02.663 --> 00:58:05.257
Patient? What patient?
Come on. you know what time it is?

583
00:58:06.300 --> 00:58:09.098
Listen. I'm sorry. I must go.
I really didn't do anything.

584
00:58:09.303 --> 00:58:11.669
- I'm sorry. Good night.
- Doctor. if we could...

585
00:58:13.974 --> 00:58:17.569
Douche bag's pinned out of his mind.
He thinks we're here to bust him.

586
00:58:20.080 --> 00:58:21.877
Dr. Isaacson. please.

587
00:58:22.082 --> 00:58:25.347
We have reason to believe your life
is in danger. grave danger.

588
00:58:26.420 --> 00:58:29.287
We think one of your patients
is trying to kill you.

589
00:58:34.562 --> 00:58:35.551
Kill me?

590
00:58:35.763 --> 00:58:39.130
I'm Agent Salinger with Interpol.
We're assisting in this manhunt.

591
00:58:39.333 --> 00:58:42.734
Why would a patient wanna kill me?
I'm an orthopedist.

592
00:58:42.937 --> 00:58:46.236
This man's a psychotic. He's already
butchered seven doctors in Europe.

593
00:58:46.440 --> 00:58:49.273
We got some serious evidence
to suggest you may be next.

594
00:58:49.476 --> 00:58:50.773
Have you ever seen this man?

595
00:58:53.147 --> 00:58:55.911
No. no. I don't think so.

596
00:58:56.116 --> 00:58:59.677
Does the name Timothy Sherwood
mean anything to you. doctor?

597
00:58:59.887 --> 00:59:02.617
No. How do you know
he's a patient of mine?

598
00:59:02.823 --> 00:59:03.881
We have his footprint.

599
00:59:04.091 --> 00:59:06.616
Yeah. the shoe was manufactured
by AGM Biomechanics...

600
00:59:06.827 --> 00:59:11.161
...exclusively for the Isaacson Institute.
model K-A-F-O 1-2-1.

601
00:59:11.365 --> 00:59:13.128
K- A-F-O 1-2-1?

602
00:59:13.334 --> 00:59:15.427
We started prescribing
that three years ago.

603
00:59:15.803 --> 00:59:17.668
We've used it on hundreds
of our patients.

604
00:59:17.871 --> 00:59:20.931
Well. then we're gonna need
to review all of your files.

605
00:59:21.542 --> 00:59:22.634
Right now?

606
00:59:22.843 --> 00:59:26.871
Doctor. we need to find this man
before he finds you.

607
00:59:28.516 --> 00:59:32.145
- What are you trying to do here. Ella?
- I'm doing my job.

608
00:59:32.354 --> 00:59:34.948
You have any idea of the shitstorm
you've gotten me into?

609
00:59:35.156 --> 00:59:37.750
- We're just trying to get to the truth.
- I get it.

610
00:59:38.393 --> 00:59:42.261
You need to remember there's what
people wanna hear. wanna believe...

611
00:59:42.464 --> 00:59:44.898
...there's everything else.
then there's the truth.

612
00:59:45.100 --> 00:59:48.399
And since when is that okay?
I can't believe you're saying this to me.

613
00:59:48.603 --> 00:59:50.662
The truth means responsibility. Arnie.

614
00:59:50.872 --> 00:59:53.841
Exactly. which is why
everyone dreads it.

615
00:59:58.947 --> 01:00:00.574
Look...

616
01:00:04.552 --> 01:00:09.251
The IBBC is using one assassin
for all their hits...

617
01:00:09.691 --> 01:00:12.489
...and we've tracked him here
to New York.

618
01:00:14.129 --> 01:00:16.791
This guy can bury them.

619
01:00:19.834 --> 01:00:22.997
They want me to put a gun
to your head.

620
01:00:23.438 --> 01:00:26.202
You don't find this guy.
and I mean quick...

621
01:00:26.408 --> 01:00:28.638
...they're gonna make me
pull the trigger.

622
01:00:33.915 --> 01:00:35.849
- Do you want dessert?
- No. thank you.

623
01:00:36.384 --> 01:00:38.011
I'd like one.

624
01:00:38.353 --> 01:00:40.947
This is a game that rewards
patience and balance.

625
01:00:41.156 --> 01:00:44.648
You must think like a man of action
and act like a man of thought.

626
01:00:56.638 --> 01:00:57.866
Gentlemen.

627
01:00:58.073 --> 01:01:00.837
<i>Sorry to disturb you at home.
I'm afraid this couldn't wait.</i>

628
01:01:01.609 --> 01:01:02.837
Yes?

629
01:01:03.044 --> 01:01:05.239
<i>Salinger was in Milan.</i>

630
01:01:05.447 --> 01:01:06.971
<i>Whitman too.</i>

631
01:01:07.182 --> 01:01:08.444
<i>They have the scent.</i>

632
01:01:08.650 --> 01:01:12.518
<i>It's only a matter of time
before they find our consultant.</i>

633
01:01:19.594 --> 01:01:21.118
Any recommendations?

634
01:01:21.329 --> 01:01:23.354
<i>I strongly advise
against doing anything...</i>

635
01:01:23.565 --> 01:01:25.931
<i>... that would heighten your exposure
right now.</i>

636
01:01:26.134 --> 01:01:28.466
<i>Wilhelm. we've leveraged ourselves
over the edge.</i>

637
01:01:28.670 --> 01:01:31.605
<i>If we don't meet the delivery date.
buyers will cancel orders...</i>

638
01:01:31.806 --> 01:01:33.137
<i>... our plans will implode...</i>

639
01:01:33.341 --> 01:01:35.708
<i>... and this bank will be left
a bill it cannot pay.</i>

640
01:01:35.911 --> 01:01:38.141
<i>Heightening exposure
is the least of our problems.</i>

641
01:01:38.347 --> 01:01:40.611
<i>I agree.
We're about to engage Calvini's sons.</i>

642
01:01:40.816 --> 01:01:42.977
<i>We can't allow anyone
to put our agenda at risk.</i>

643
01:01:43.185 --> 01:01:45.483
<i>We must sever all ties
with the consultant.</i>

644
01:01:45.688 --> 01:01:47.849
<i>Consider the mark. gentlemen.</i>

645
01:01:48.057 --> 01:01:52.994
<i>Doing this could be
a very messy affair.</i>

646
01:01:53.195 --> 01:01:55.425
<i>Well. then make it one.</i>

647
01:01:55.631 --> 01:01:58.225
<i>I don't know why you pay me
to advise on these matters.</i>

648
01:01:58.434 --> 01:02:02.302
<i>It is clear that you don't want my
counsel. only my corroboration.</i>

649
01:02:02.505 --> 01:02:06.100
<i>Really. Wilhelm. We've had
just about all we can take of you.</i>

650
01:02:06.308 --> 01:02:11.268
<i>Yes. I've had about all I can take
of myself.</i>

651
01:02:12.214 --> 01:02:14.512
<i>How would you like us to proceed?</i>

652
01:02:19.288 --> 01:02:23.019
Cassian. what does one do when
there's no way out of a situation?

653
01:02:23.425 --> 01:02:25.290
If there's no way out...

654
01:02:26.495 --> 01:02:29.862
...the best thing is
to find a way further in.

655
01:02:49.785 --> 01:02:52.549
- Fucking disgusting. you know that?
- What are you. my mother?

656
01:02:52.755 --> 01:02:55.656
No. but I could be your old man
for all you know. asshole.

657
01:03:06.769 --> 01:03:08.327
Hey. doc.

658
01:03:10.739 --> 01:03:12.138
Gabriel Hansen?

659
01:03:12.875 --> 01:03:16.436
I don't know.
My associate handled this.

660
01:03:17.346 --> 01:03:20.076
Well. the address
is a post-office box...

661
01:03:20.950 --> 01:03:23.475
...and he paid cash
for all of his medical bills.

662
01:03:24.920 --> 01:03:28.549
There are no diagnostic photos.
Why?

663
01:03:30.559 --> 01:03:32.322
- I don't know.
- Is there a number?

664
01:03:32.528 --> 01:03:38.296
Yeah. 212-157-6421.

665
01:03:44.173 --> 01:03:45.162
It's a dead line.

666
01:03:51.348 --> 01:03:53.578
I'll put a call in to Hubby.
have her run it down.

667
01:03:53.783 --> 01:03:56.581
See if we can't get a crack warrant
for the P.O. Box in Jersey.

668
01:04:01.191 --> 01:04:04.683
What do all these GT's
next to the appointment entries mean?

669
01:04:05.328 --> 01:04:07.956
We have a kickback account
with Go Taxi...

670
01:04:08.465 --> 01:04:11.229
...and they indicate when we
use their service for a patient.

671
01:04:14.037 --> 01:04:15.732
<i>Hey. Hubb says you caught a lead.</i>

672
01:04:15.939 --> 01:04:17.873
Yeah. we've got an address.
We're en route.

673
01:04:18.074 --> 01:04:19.666
<i>- What is it?
- Well. it could be him.</i>

674
01:04:19.876 --> 01:04:21.104
<i>- Really?
- Yeah.</i>

675
01:04:21.311 --> 01:04:24.144
<i>Well. they gotta bring him in now.
This is our last shot.</i>

676
01:04:24.347 --> 01:04:25.905
What do you mean. "our last shot"?

677
01:04:26.116 --> 01:04:28.983
<i>Arnie and I had it out last night.
and our clock's run out.</i>

678
01:04:29.519 --> 01:04:33.250
<i>If we don't get this guy right now.
it's over.</i>

679
01:04:35.058 --> 01:04:37.322
Well. it better be him. then.

680
01:04:49.272 --> 01:04:51.604
I'm here. Yeah.

681
01:04:54.945 --> 01:04:55.934
I know that.

682
01:04:56.146 --> 01:04:57.943
This is definitely the right address?

683
01:04:58.148 --> 01:05:02.141
Checked the log myself. This is where
they dropped him off every time.

684
01:05:03.386 --> 01:05:05.377
Well. he could be anywhere.

685
01:05:08.325 --> 01:05:10.987
- What do you think he was doing?
- Beats the shit out of me.

686
01:05:11.194 --> 01:05:12.252
It's a big. empty lot.

687
01:05:12.462 --> 01:05:15.329
Well. I'm starving. I'm gonna
get something. You want anything?

688
01:05:15.532 --> 01:05:16.521
Yeah. a coffee. black.

689
01:05:16.733 --> 01:05:19.099
I'm going back down to
headquarters after this.

690
01:05:19.302 --> 01:05:21.133
Okay. all right.

691
01:05:28.778 --> 01:05:29.745
Right. bye.

692
01:05:29.946 --> 01:05:32.005
How long do you think
this has been like this?

693
01:05:32.215 --> 01:05:34.046
I don't know. but we need to find out.

694
01:05:34.250 --> 01:05:36.081
The doctor's records say
the last time...

695
01:05:36.286 --> 01:05:39.153
...somebody got dropped off here
was five weeks ago.

696
01:05:39.756 --> 01:05:42.623
I mean. there's not even
a temporary office or anything.

697
01:05:43.293 --> 01:05:45.284
- How you doing?
- How you doing?

698
01:06:02.113 --> 01:06:04.809
Son of a bitch.

699
01:06:10.287 --> 01:06:11.311
What's the matter?

700
01:06:11.522 --> 01:06:14.184
I just made our perp.
Eleven o'clock. blue overcoat.

701
01:06:16.861 --> 01:06:19.421
- You sure that's him?
- A hundred percent.

702
01:06:20.097 --> 01:06:21.928
- Where did he come from?
- Shit if I know.

703
01:06:22.133 --> 01:06:24.863
I'm at the counter and
I see him rolling past the window.

704
01:06:25.069 --> 01:06:26.434
- Wanna go for the collar?
- No.

705
01:06:26.637 --> 01:06:29.265
We tail him. find out where he sleeps.
then take him down.

706
01:06:29.473 --> 01:06:32.408
A. B. C. Keep the box tight.

707
01:07:50.454 --> 01:07:55.221
<i>- Five-oh-two-six. Designator?
- Samuel Koppler.</i>

708
01:07:57.027 --> 01:07:58.255
<i>Message:</i>

709
01:07:58.963 --> 01:08:01.830
<i>Your uncle
wishes to see you immediately.</i>

710
01:08:02.032 --> 01:08:03.431
<i>Response?</i>

711
01:08:03.634 --> 01:08:08.367
The Guggenheim. fifth floor
of the rotunda. 40 minutes.

712
01:08:54.019 --> 01:08:55.543
- Hi. how you doing?
- Hello.

713
01:08:55.754 --> 01:08:57.984
N.Y.P.D. I need to
speak to your security chief.

714
01:08:58.190 --> 01:08:59.589
Okay. one moment.

715
01:09:00.692 --> 01:09:02.250
Rick?

716
01:09:02.894 --> 01:09:06.227
How you doing? Detective Ornelas.
I need to be able to clear security.

717
01:09:06.431 --> 01:09:07.864
- Okay.
- Thanks.

718
01:09:13.071 --> 01:09:14.732
We're clear.

719
01:09:46.238 --> 01:09:48.570
Directly behind me.

720
01:09:56.381 --> 01:09:58.212
There you go. Thank you.

721
01:10:49.135 --> 01:10:51.262
Who's the old scag
sitting next to him?

722
01:10:51.470 --> 01:10:54.667
I don't know. but I saw him at the
bank's headquarters in Luxembourg.

723
01:10:55.308 --> 01:10:57.970
You don't look well today.

724
01:10:58.411 --> 01:11:00.879
We all begin better than we end.

725
01:11:01.681 --> 01:11:04.013
What would you prefer your ending
to be like?

726
01:11:04.216 --> 01:11:09.153
Oh. more purposeful.
and certainly more climactic.

727
01:11:09.655 --> 01:11:11.247
A finale.

728
01:11:11.891 --> 01:11:13.483
A finale.

729
01:11:13.693 --> 01:11:17.220
Circumstances can always
be arranged.

730
01:11:18.230 --> 01:11:20.095
As much as the thought
appeals to me...

731
01:11:20.299 --> 01:11:23.962
...I'm afraid your consideration
is needed elsewhere.

732
01:11:24.837 --> 01:11:27.362
- What is this?
- Salinger.

733
01:11:27.940 --> 01:11:30.773
The method and manner
is entirely up to you.

734
01:11:30.976 --> 01:11:36.175
Your principle would simply like him
to vanish without a trace.

735
01:11:38.451 --> 01:11:41.750
- Any other provisions?
- Yes.

736
01:11:41.954 --> 01:11:43.251
No mistakes.

737
01:11:46.592 --> 01:11:48.389
I'll follow.

738
01:11:53.599 --> 01:11:56.898
- Where's Iggy going?
- Following a new lead.

739
01:12:25.698 --> 01:12:27.063
Shit.

740
01:12:27.266 --> 01:12:28.631
We gotta go.

741
01:12:30.269 --> 01:12:33.364
N.Y.P.D. Lock your hands
behind your head.

742
01:12:37.411 --> 01:12:38.537
Do it now.

743
01:12:39.146 --> 01:12:40.875
They'll never let you bring me in.

744
01:12:41.081 --> 01:12:43.140
Do it. or I'll take you down.

745
01:12:46.353 --> 01:12:47.615
- Cuffs.
- On the belt.

746
01:12:58.131 --> 01:12:59.496
There's a guy right up there.

747
01:13:27.227 --> 01:13:29.320
- Where'd he...?
- Up there! Up there!

748
01:13:40.006 --> 01:13:40.995
Get down!

749
01:13:47.814 --> 01:13:49.679
- God! Oh. my God!
- It's okay.

750
01:13:52.452 --> 01:13:53.441
Down there.

751
01:14:03.296 --> 01:14:05.127
Shit.

752
01:14:25.385 --> 01:14:26.374
Drop the gun.

753
01:14:27.687 --> 01:14:31.418
- If I drop the gun. we'll both die.
- I said. drop the gun!

754
01:14:31.625 --> 01:14:35.584
They're here for me but they'll kill
you too. Now help me get this off.

755
01:14:37.130 --> 01:14:38.324
I can't breathe.

756
01:15:01.289 --> 01:15:03.018
Stairs.

757
01:15:15.069 --> 01:15:16.969
- Fuck.
- You okay?

758
01:15:20.107 --> 01:15:21.574
The ramp is the only way out.

759
01:17:36.845 --> 01:17:38.472
Hey.

760
01:17:40.148 --> 01:17:42.708
Don't you fucking dare.

761
01:18:35.771 --> 01:18:37.966
<i>I'm calling from the dark side.</i>

762
01:18:38.173 --> 01:18:41.836
<i>- Sorry. Sorry. Sorry.
- I'm calling from the...</i>

763
01:19:19.682 --> 01:19:20.979
Get back.

764
01:19:41.404 --> 01:19:43.065
I told you.

765
01:19:45.107 --> 01:19:47.473
What? You told me what?

766
01:19:49.011 --> 01:19:51.912
They'd never let you bring me in.

767
01:20:18.074 --> 01:20:19.063
Fuck. fuck.

768
01:20:29.185 --> 01:20:31.449
<i>Move away from the building.</i>

769
01:20:31.654 --> 01:20:35.522
<i>Can everybody please
move away from the building?</i>

770
01:20:54.110 --> 01:20:56.078
They know you're coming.
We gotta hurry.

771
01:20:56.279 --> 01:20:59.612
- Where'd they find him?
- Sitting on a bench near the reservoir.

772
01:21:00.249 --> 01:21:03.377
- Has he said anything yet?
- Nothing. He's pretty shaken up.

773
01:21:03.586 --> 01:21:07.386
- Who else knows he's here?
- Everyone. Nothing I could do.

774
01:21:07.590 --> 01:21:09.990
Heavies from the Bureau
and Justice are on their way.

775
01:21:10.192 --> 01:21:11.887
<i>... with an unidentified third man.</i>

776
01:21:12.094 --> 01:21:14.824
- How long do I have?
- Five. 10 minutes. max.

777
01:21:15.031 --> 01:21:17.556
<i>... wanted for questioning
in an ongoing investigation.</i>

778
01:21:17.867 --> 01:21:23.170
<i>Now. a Guggenheim employee tells me
that while they were in the museum...</i>

779
01:21:59.376 --> 01:22:01.571
This isn't over.

780
01:22:19.663 --> 01:22:21.290
Are you sure about this?

781
01:22:27.204 --> 01:22:28.193
Just read it.

782
01:22:43.653 --> 01:22:45.644
- They recognize you?
- Don't think so.

783
01:22:50.127 --> 01:22:52.095
Back it up!

784
01:23:33.604 --> 01:23:35.731
<i>...screens came crashing down.
- How you doing?</i>

785
01:23:35.940 --> 01:23:39.273
<i>- There was glass everywhere.
- As compared to what?</i>

786
01:23:39.477 --> 01:23:41.308
<i>And just on the ground.</i>

787
01:23:41.512 --> 01:23:44.242
<i>When you heard all of this
commotion. did you think...?</i>

788
01:23:44.482 --> 01:23:46.416
Anything you need. Ellie.
just let me know.

789
01:23:46.617 --> 01:23:48.642
<i>- Thanks.
- I just heard gunshots.</i>

790
01:23:48.853 --> 01:23:50.980
<i>And people were hit
and screaming...</i>

791
01:23:51.189 --> 01:23:53.419
<i>... and people just started running
out the door...</i>

792
01:23:53.624 --> 01:23:55.353
<i>... and I didn't know
what was going on.</i>

793
01:23:55.560 --> 01:23:56.549
You okay?

794
01:23:57.328 --> 01:23:58.852
Yeah.

795
01:24:00.731 --> 01:24:02.824
You flip this guy.

796
01:24:03.301 --> 01:24:06.236
You make sure my partner
wasn't killed for nothing.

797
01:24:06.437 --> 01:24:10.168
<i>I know that... I think random people
were going down and...</i>

798
01:24:10.374 --> 01:24:14.902
<i>I mean. there was police running up
as other people were going down.</i>

799
01:24:27.425 --> 01:24:28.949
You ready for this?

800
01:25:05.630 --> 01:25:08.121
Good evening. Colonel Wexler.

801
01:25:09.934 --> 01:25:12.562
I'm Agent Louis Salinger.

802
01:25:13.371 --> 01:25:15.532
I know who you are.

803
01:25:17.408 --> 01:25:19.501
Of course you do.

804
01:25:21.546 --> 01:25:23.878
I was at the Guggenheim
this afternoon.

805
01:25:26.117 --> 01:25:27.709
<i>The assassin you met with...</i>

806
01:25:29.387 --> 01:25:31.480
<i>... I know you were his handler.</i>

807
01:25:31.689 --> 01:25:34.852
I know you arranged for him
to be killed at the behest of the bank...

808
01:25:35.059 --> 01:25:37.254
...because I was obviously
getting too close.

809
01:25:40.565 --> 01:25:43.261
But if a hit team at the Guggenheim
is what happens...

810
01:25:43.468 --> 01:25:46.266
...because I was
getting too close to him...

811
01:25:48.840 --> 01:25:52.537
...what do you think the bank'll do
when it realizes how close I am to you?

812
01:25:52.744 --> 01:25:57.306
Death comes for us all.
Agent Salinger.

813
01:25:58.050 --> 01:26:00.109
But based on everything
I've read about you...

814
01:26:00.319 --> 01:26:02.014
...you seem like the kind of man...

815
01:26:02.221 --> 01:26:05.122
...who aspired to die
for something more than this.

816
01:26:06.925 --> 01:26:11.419
Well. this is the difference
between truth and fiction.

817
01:26:12.764 --> 01:26:15.028
Fiction has to make sense.

818
01:26:17.803 --> 01:26:19.703
I'm confused. colonel.

819
01:26:22.874 --> 01:26:25.069
Why would a tried
and true communist...

820
01:26:26.178 --> 01:26:28.544
...a hardliner that spent 30 years
in the Stasi...

821
01:26:28.747 --> 01:26:30.908
...fighting against the evils
of capitalism...

822
01:26:31.617 --> 01:26:34.780
Why would this man waste his
final days working for an institution...

823
01:26:34.987 --> 01:26:38.150
...that was the very embodiment
of everything he once despised?

824
01:26:41.193 --> 01:26:44.060
You dedicated your life
to the communist ideal.

825
01:26:46.498 --> 01:26:49.865
You sacrificed everything
for the good of the party.

826
01:26:51.403 --> 01:26:52.734
For what?

827
01:26:56.475 --> 01:26:59.103
You lost your wife to betrayal...

828
01:26:59.745 --> 01:27:02.236
...your daughter to suicide...

829
01:27:03.615 --> 01:27:06.846
...and when the Wall fell.
your whole life fell apart with it.

830
01:27:07.152 --> 01:27:09.416
You know nothing about me.

831
01:27:09.988 --> 01:27:12.855
I was lost long before the Wall fell.

832
01:27:14.092 --> 01:27:18.791
I was once destined to become
a man much like yourself.

833
01:27:19.231 --> 01:27:21.028
True-hearted...

834
01:27:21.366 --> 01:27:23.334
...determined...

835
01:27:23.535 --> 01:27:25.503
...full of purpose.

836
01:27:26.505 --> 01:27:28.405
But...

837
01:27:28.874 --> 01:27:31.604
...character is easier kept
than recovered.

838
01:27:32.844 --> 01:27:36.712
We cannot control
the things life does to us.

839
01:27:37.382 --> 01:27:41.318
They are done before you know it.
and once they are done...

840
01:27:42.721 --> 01:27:44.882
...they make you do other things...

841
01:27:45.490 --> 01:27:48.687
...until at last.
everything comes between you...

842
01:27:49.728 --> 01:27:52.219
...and the man you wanted to be.

843
01:27:54.166 --> 01:27:55.634
No.

844
01:27:57.570 --> 01:28:00.733
We all have choices in life.
You made yours.

845
01:28:08.147 --> 01:28:09.944
Sometimes a man
can meet his destiny...

846
01:28:10.149 --> 01:28:11.980
...on the road he took to avoid it.

847
01:28:15.221 --> 01:28:17.951
Skarssen and that bank need to
answer for what they've done.

848
01:28:18.157 --> 01:28:20.125
They have to be brought to justice.

849
01:28:20.326 --> 01:28:22.260
You can help me do that.

850
01:28:22.595 --> 01:28:24.392
Justice...

851
01:28:25.231 --> 01:28:27.165
...is not possible.

852
01:28:27.834 --> 01:28:29.301
Why not?

853
01:28:29.769 --> 01:28:32.260
Because. Agent Salinger...

854
01:28:32.472 --> 01:28:36.408
...your idea of justice is an illusion.

855
01:28:37.176 --> 01:28:39.701
<i>Understand the very system
that you serve and protect...</i>

856
01:28:39.912 --> 01:28:43.439
<i>... will never allow anything to happen
to Skarssen or the bank.</i>

857
01:28:44.050 --> 01:28:45.608
On the contrary.

858
01:28:46.018 --> 01:28:50.079
The system guarantees
the IBBC's safety...

859
01:28:50.523 --> 01:28:53.754
...because everyone is involved.

860
01:28:54.560 --> 01:28:56.494
What do you mean. "everyone"?

861
01:28:59.332 --> 01:29:00.765
Hezbollah.

862
01:29:01.300 --> 01:29:03.234
CIA.

863
01:29:03.736 --> 01:29:05.431
The Columbian drug cartels.

864
01:29:05.838 --> 01:29:07.999
Russian organized crime.

865
01:29:08.207 --> 01:29:11.643
Governments of Iran. Germany.
China. your government.

866
01:29:11.878 --> 01:29:14.938
Every multinational corporation.
every one.

867
01:29:15.381 --> 01:29:19.681
They all need banks like the IBBC...

868
01:29:19.886 --> 01:29:24.755
...so that they can operate
within the black and gray latitudes.

869
01:29:25.158 --> 01:29:27.183
And this is why
your investigative efforts...

870
01:29:27.393 --> 01:29:30.954
...have either been ignored
or undermined...

871
01:29:31.164 --> 01:29:34.292
...and why you and I
will be quietly disposed of...

872
01:29:35.301 --> 01:29:40.329
...before any case against the bank
ever reaches a court of law.

873
01:29:46.479 --> 01:29:48.504
<i>So. what are we all
supposed to do?</i>

874
01:29:51.851 --> 01:29:54.115
We just supposed to give up...

875
01:29:54.420 --> 01:29:57.184
...and accept that
this is the way of the world?

876
01:30:01.661 --> 01:30:03.424
I'm not gonna do that.

877
01:30:04.864 --> 01:30:08.028
I still believe... I know...

878
01:30:08.235 --> 01:30:11.636
...that there has to be a way
to bring down this bank...

879
01:30:12.272 --> 01:30:14.638
...and you are gonna help me.

880
01:30:21.782 --> 01:30:23.943
You understand...

881
01:30:25.319 --> 01:30:29.050
...if you really want to
stop the IBBC...

882
01:30:29.790 --> 01:30:34.955
...you won't be able to do it within the
boundaries of your system of justice.

883
01:30:35.596 --> 01:30:37.962
You will have to go outside.

884
01:30:38.732 --> 01:30:40.290
Once you do...

885
01:30:41.969 --> 01:30:45.461
...there will always be
collateral damage.

886
01:30:50.210 --> 01:30:51.939
<i>Yes.</i>

887
01:30:53.013 --> 01:30:57.416
<i>Should you sacrifice your own ideals
for the greater good?</i>

888
01:30:58.585 --> 01:31:02.385
That's a difficult choice.
one I understand all too well...

889
01:31:03.323 --> 01:31:05.553
...but as you so eloquently put it...

890
01:31:05.993 --> 01:31:09.326
...sometimes a man
can meet his destiny...

891
01:31:09.530 --> 01:31:12.931
...on the road he took to avoid it.

892
01:31:24.845 --> 01:31:25.937
What?

893
01:31:26.146 --> 01:31:27.374
What are you doing?

894
01:31:28.015 --> 01:31:29.915
I think it's time for you to leave.

895
01:31:30.584 --> 01:31:35.283
- Leave? What are you talking about?
- You know what I'm talking about.

896
01:31:38.825 --> 01:31:40.656
No way. Lou.

897
01:31:40.861 --> 01:31:43.728
No fucking way.
You've already got him turned.

898
01:31:43.931 --> 01:31:47.332
Now go back in there
and get him to come in on his own.

899
01:31:47.868 --> 01:31:50.894
We can use everything.
We'll blow this whole thing wide open.

900
01:31:51.104 --> 01:31:53.402
- I don't think so.
- Why not?

901
01:31:53.607 --> 01:31:55.598
I'm not gonna make
the same mistake twice.

902
01:31:55.809 --> 01:31:59.370
- I can protect him. Lou.
- No. you can't. They'll get to him.

903
01:31:59.580 --> 01:32:01.138
If they can't. they'll get to you.

904
01:32:01.348 --> 01:32:03.748
If they can't get to you.
they'll get to your family.

905
01:32:16.463 --> 01:32:18.625
I can't just walk away from this.

906
01:32:19.934 --> 01:32:22.732
You're walking away
so I don't have to.

907
01:32:31.679 --> 01:32:33.112
How can you trust him?

908
01:32:33.581 --> 01:32:36.709
That relic in there
is looking for redemption.

909
01:32:36.918 --> 01:32:38.943
I'm the only one
who can give it to him.

910
01:32:40.021 --> 01:32:42.854
Then who gives it to you
when this is all over?

911
01:32:44.559 --> 01:32:46.618
You need to cut me loose.

912
01:32:49.230 --> 01:32:51.960
Tell them I escaped from custody.
whatever you have to.

913
01:32:52.166 --> 01:32:54.157
Just use my history.
They'll believe you.

914
01:32:54.369 --> 01:32:56.633
- I don't know.
- Ella. listen to me.

915
01:32:58.506 --> 01:32:59.871
Sometimes the hardest thing...

916
01:33:00.074 --> 01:33:03.066
...is to know which bridge to cross
and which to burn.

917
01:33:07.482 --> 01:33:09.677
I'm the one you burn.

918
01:34:09.277 --> 01:34:11.336
We've been waiting here
for an hour.

919
01:34:11.546 --> 01:34:15.346
I'm sorry. Martin. but none of us
have been able to reach them.

920
01:34:15.917 --> 01:34:20.411
Unfortunately. Mario and Enzo Calvini
are not known for their punctuality.

921
01:34:20.621 --> 01:34:22.452
They do realize this is the closing?

922
01:34:45.247 --> 01:34:46.578
Mr. White...

923
01:34:46.782 --> 01:34:50.240
...I've been instructed to escort you
and your associates from the building.

924
01:34:50.452 --> 01:34:52.511
Please gather your materials
and come with me.

925
01:34:52.721 --> 01:34:56.248
- Instructed by whom?
- Please. if you could just comply.

926
01:35:18.480 --> 01:35:21.108
Our father
never trusted these people.

927
01:35:22.751 --> 01:35:25.879
Thank you for telling us the truth.

928
01:35:29.491 --> 01:35:31.322
Had you not come forward...

929
01:35:31.527 --> 01:35:33.927
...we would have made
a terrible mistake today.

930
01:35:34.129 --> 01:35:36.791
I'm just glad I could be of service.

931
01:35:43.138 --> 01:35:46.801
I don't know. Jonas. I was told nothing.
I was simply thrown out.

932
01:35:47.276 --> 01:35:49.039
<i>They know.</i>

933
01:35:55.517 --> 01:35:59.817
Look. I can't discuss this right now.
I'll call you when I'm in the air.

934
01:36:25.414 --> 01:36:27.905
<i>Welcome to World News.
I'm Tristana Moore.</i>

935
01:36:28.116 --> 01:36:31.517
<i>We're live today in the
Democratic Republic of Niberia.</i>

936
01:36:31.720 --> 01:36:34.746
<i>As we go on air. we're getting reports
that thousands of troops...</i>

937
01:36:34.957 --> 01:36:38.586
<i>... loyal to General Charles Motomba's
Revolutionary Freedom Front...</i>

938
01:36:38.794 --> 01:36:41.354
<i>... are moving towards
the capital of Denue.</i>

939
01:36:41.563 --> 01:36:44.499
<i>According to eyewitnesses.
several explosions have been heard...</i>

940
01:36:44.701 --> 01:36:48.694
<i>... and there've been heavy outbreaks
of gunfire in many parts of the city.</i>

941
01:36:48.905 --> 01:36:51.567
<i>The people of Niberia
have suffered greatly.</i>

942
01:36:51.774 --> 01:36:55.210
<i>It is time to begin a new chapter
in our country's history.</i>

943
01:36:55.411 --> 01:36:58.278
<i>We will not stop
until national liberation...</i>

944
01:36:58.481 --> 01:37:00.949
<i>... and the restoration of nationhood...</i>

945
01:37:05.755 --> 01:37:06.779
News about Martin?

946
01:37:07.757 --> 01:37:10.248
He didn't show up at his hotel
or at the airport.

947
01:37:10.460 --> 01:37:15.022
The Italian police have been unable
to locate his car or driver.

948
01:37:15.231 --> 01:37:18.894
I think Enzo and Mario Calvini
are sending us a message.

949
01:37:19.102 --> 01:37:21.468
How could they possibly
have found out?

950
01:37:25.241 --> 01:37:27.766
This is precisely
what we pay you to know.

951
01:37:27.977 --> 01:37:29.467
We're out of time and options.

952
01:37:29.879 --> 01:37:33.781
- We must make the deal with Sunay.
- How can we trust this man?

953
01:37:33.983 --> 01:37:37.111
The Israeli government
is his biggest customer.

954
01:37:37.320 --> 01:37:38.412
Why would he agree...

955
01:37:38.621 --> 01:37:42.182
...to help us provide missiles
to the Iranians and the Syrians...

956
01:37:42.392 --> 01:37:45.122
...that have a first-strike capability
against the Israelis?

957
01:37:45.328 --> 01:37:47.796
I know Sunay.
I believe he has every intention...

958
01:37:47.997 --> 01:37:49.828
...of selling you
the guidance systems...

959
01:37:50.266 --> 01:37:52.427
...because he's already provided
the Israelis...

960
01:37:52.635 --> 01:37:55.468
...with the countermeasures
to defeat them.

961
01:37:57.373 --> 01:38:00.171
Would the Turk really play
such a dangerous game?

962
01:38:01.678 --> 01:38:03.305
We are.

963
01:38:04.447 --> 01:38:06.711
The only way we can make this work...

964
01:38:06.916 --> 01:38:07.905
...is to guarantee...

965
01:38:08.117 --> 01:38:10.847
...that Sunay keeps this information
in complete confidence.

966
01:38:11.054 --> 01:38:14.990
If our buyers find out the missiles are
worthless. they'll pull all their orders...

967
01:38:15.191 --> 01:38:17.523
...and this bank will be left insolvent.

968
01:38:18.027 --> 01:38:19.961
Have him here
by tomorrow afternoon.

969
01:38:20.163 --> 01:38:23.394
Tomorrow he's going to
a funeral service for his cousin.

970
01:38:23.599 --> 01:38:25.464
He'll be unavailable till Monday.

971
01:38:26.102 --> 01:38:29.196
Unless of course.
you'd be willing to attend.

972
01:38:30.673 --> 01:38:32.470
Make the call.

973
01:38:34.944 --> 01:38:37.242
Get me Ahmet Sunay.

974
01:38:44.053 --> 01:38:46.021
It's tomorrow.

975
01:39:27.231 --> 01:39:29.791
It's right there.
Do you want to be escorted?

976
01:39:30.000 --> 01:39:31.433
We'll be fine. thank you.

977
01:39:37.408 --> 01:39:38.841
The Sunay funeral. please.

978
01:39:39.043 --> 01:39:41.341
It will be over soon.
You may wait here.

979
01:39:41.545 --> 01:39:45.538
- Is there a bathroom I could use?
- Just over there.

980
01:39:45.749 --> 01:39:48.684
- I won't be a moment.
- Right.

981
01:39:55.192 --> 01:39:57.353
- The signal?
- Good.

982
01:39:57.561 --> 01:39:58.926
<i>The Sunay funeral. please.</i>

983
01:39:59.563 --> 01:40:03.090
- Where'd you put the spike?
- Inside the lapel of his jacket.

984
01:40:04.301 --> 01:40:05.359
The lawyer?

985
01:40:06.570 --> 01:40:08.128
White?

986
01:40:08.372 --> 01:40:09.396
He's gone.

987
01:40:11.141 --> 01:40:15.009
I told you. there will always
be collateral damage...

988
01:40:15.212 --> 01:40:17.476
...when you take matters
into your own hands.

989
01:40:19.917 --> 01:40:20.941
Your plan is working.

990
01:40:21.885 --> 01:40:24.115
It has left Skarssen
with only one option.

991
01:40:24.321 --> 01:40:28.018
Record the conversation
and you'll gain your end.

992
01:40:30.194 --> 01:40:33.721
Sure they'll talk about Sunay's deal
with Israel and the countermeasures?

993
01:40:33.931 --> 01:40:35.262
It is the key issue.

994
01:40:35.466 --> 01:40:37.400
Once you let the Iranians
and Syrians...

995
01:40:37.601 --> 01:40:42.163
...hear that the missiles are completely
useless against the Israelis...

996
01:40:42.673 --> 01:40:48.509
...they will cancel their orders
and the IBBC will collapse.

997
01:40:57.187 --> 01:40:59.280
- Wilhelm.
- Ahmet.

998
01:40:59.790 --> 01:41:01.087
It's been a long time.

999
01:41:01.458 --> 01:41:02.447
<i>Yes.</i>

1000
01:41:02.659 --> 01:41:04.524
<i>My sympathies for the loss
of your cousin.</i>

1001
01:41:04.728 --> 01:41:05.957
Thank you.

1002
01:41:06.164 --> 01:41:08.758
Jonas Skarssen. Ahmet Sunay.

1003
01:41:08.967 --> 01:41:13.131
If you'd simply come to me in the
beginning. it would have been better.

1004
01:41:15.974 --> 01:41:17.771
<i>Midday prayers will begin soon.</i>

1005
01:41:17.976 --> 01:41:20.501
Should take a short time
to settle on the broad strokes.

1006
01:41:20.712 --> 01:41:22.577
<i>The rest can be sorted out
at your leisure.</i>

1007
01:41:22.780 --> 01:41:23.769
<i>We have 10 minutes.</i>

1008
01:41:35.894 --> 01:41:39.227
Wilhelm. would you mind
if I spoke to Mr. Sunay alone?

1009
01:41:44.469 --> 01:41:48.098
I believe I understand
the particulars of your situation.

1010
01:41:48.306 --> 01:41:51.139
<i>Perhaps we should discuss this
in a more private place.</i>

1011
01:41:51.342 --> 01:41:53.003
<i>Yes. of course.</i>

1012
01:41:53.411 --> 01:41:56.039
<i>Allow me to show you something
very special.</i>

1013
01:41:56.247 --> 01:42:00.013
<i>Something that very few outsiders
know exists.</i>

1014
01:42:01.519 --> 01:42:06.218
<i>It's my understanding that the product
you purchased are the XW-41 s.</i>

1015
01:42:06.691 --> 01:42:07.715
After you.

1016
01:42:07.926 --> 01:42:10.258
<i>Yes. Forty-two hundred units.</i>

1017
01:42:12.530 --> 01:42:15.363
What kind of guidance
are they currently equipped...?

1018
01:42:20.605 --> 01:42:23.597
<i>They all need to be upgraded
with VOLCON systems.</i>

1019
01:42:24.409 --> 01:42:26.070
<i>Launch platforms?</i>

1020
01:42:26.277 --> 01:42:28.837
<i>Ground-based vehicles
and fixed-wing aircraft.</i>

1021
01:42:39.290 --> 01:42:41.850
So you understand
I have a terminal deadline.

1022
01:42:42.060 --> 01:42:43.857
First of February. yes.

1023
01:42:44.062 --> 01:42:45.962
<i>- Can you meet it?
- To be sure.</i>

1024
01:42:46.164 --> 01:42:49.759
<i>But you must arrange for the
end-user certificates. transport...</i>

1025
01:42:49.968 --> 01:42:51.492
<i>We'll arrange for it all.</i>

1026
01:42:51.703 --> 01:42:53.136
<i>Where would the work be done?</i>

1027
01:42:53.338 --> 01:42:56.205
<i>Cyprus. I've a facility there.</i>

1028
01:42:57.642 --> 01:43:01.203
<i>We would start retrofitting the worms
within a day of their arrival.</i>

1029
01:43:01.412 --> 01:43:04.472
<i>So if you deliver them to me
within the next two weeks...</i>

1030
01:43:04.682 --> 01:43:06.616
<i>... we'll meet your deadline.</i>

1031
01:43:19.198 --> 01:43:22.463
I'm concerned that we limit any and all
knowledge of your involvement.

1032
01:43:23.168 --> 01:43:26.569
<i>If we structure my involvement
through a thick veil of shells...</i>

1033
01:43:27.773 --> 01:43:29.741
<i>... I don't foresee any complications.</i>

1034
01:43:31.176 --> 01:43:33.906
- Sorry?
- You. Come here now.

1035
01:43:34.113 --> 01:43:37.139
<i>Usually we would involve
our import partners from Russia.</i>

1036
01:43:37.583 --> 01:43:39.016
What? I'm just a tourist.

1037
01:43:39.218 --> 01:43:41.812
- Now. you must leave.
- Could you get that light out of...?

1038
01:43:42.021 --> 01:43:44.649
Get your fucking...

1039
01:43:46.825 --> 01:43:50.317
So. shall we discuss numbers?

1040
01:43:50.763 --> 01:43:52.458
There is a more salient deal point...

1041
01:43:52.665 --> 01:43:55.463
...that needs to be resolved
before we can do that.

1042
01:43:55.668 --> 01:43:57.465
<i>And what point is that?</i>

1043
01:43:58.470 --> 01:44:00.700
<i>The point of fidelity.</i>

1044
01:44:07.880 --> 01:44:09.905
I know you provided
the Israeli government...

1045
01:44:10.115 --> 01:44:13.050
...with the countermeasures
to this guidance system.

1046
01:44:21.160 --> 01:44:23.219
Last year alone...

1047
01:44:23.429 --> 01:44:26.990
...I did more than 300 million
in business with the Israelis.

1048
01:44:30.703 --> 01:44:33.001
I would never put that at risk.

1049
01:44:33.205 --> 01:44:37.403
How can I trust you not to divulge
this information to anyone else?

1050
01:44:38.377 --> 01:44:40.902
It's mutual interest. not trust...

1051
01:44:41.347 --> 01:44:43.975
...that will be the bond
of our relationship.

1052
01:44:47.753 --> 01:44:50.586
Your compensation will be held
in an escrow account.

1053
01:44:51.824 --> 01:44:54.019
<i>... released until our clients pay
in full.</i>

1054
01:44:54.727 --> 01:44:56.058
And those are the terms.

1055
01:44:58.831 --> 01:45:00.458
<i>The payout structure...</i>

1056
01:45:02.868 --> 01:45:05.166
<i>The transfers will be begun
by tomorrow morning.</i>

1057
01:45:05.371 --> 01:45:08.863
<i>Ehames will contact you with
the number for the escrow account.</i>

1058
01:45:14.179 --> 01:45:17.171
So ends the bloody business
of the day.

1059
01:45:30.029 --> 01:45:32.395
We're closed. I need you and Ehames
here tomorrow...

1060
01:45:32.599 --> 01:45:35.159
...to work out all the details
with Sunay's people.

1061
01:45:35.568 --> 01:45:38.298
Yes. We're on our way home.

1062
01:45:46.146 --> 01:45:47.135
Wilhelm?

1063
01:45:50.150 --> 01:45:51.549
Wake up.

1064
01:48:52.600 --> 01:48:53.589
Who are you?

1065
01:48:55.836 --> 01:48:57.599
I'm Louis Salinger.

1066
01:49:07.581 --> 01:49:10.277
You don't have the authority
to arrest me.

1067
01:49:12.553 --> 01:49:15.249
Who said anything
about arresting you?

1068
01:49:19.593 --> 01:49:23.324
- What do you want?
- I want some fucking justice.

1069
01:49:23.530 --> 01:49:27.227
Wait. wait. Wait.
Executing me won't change anything.

1070
01:49:27.434 --> 01:49:29.925
There will be 100 other bankers
to take my place.

1071
01:49:30.137 --> 01:49:33.129
Everything will continue.

1072
01:49:33.340 --> 01:49:39.279
The only thing you'll succeed in doing
is to satisfy your own blood lust.

1073
01:49:44.218 --> 01:49:45.651
And you know it.

1074
01:50:40.308 --> 01:50:42.936
With compliments of Enzo
and Mario Calvini.

1075
01:50:58.093 --> 01:50:59.560
Thank you.

1076
01:51:00.305 --> 01:52:00.541
